["er.request/1",{"arguments":{"body":"# Store and executor executable contracts\n\nApproved stages 4–5 of the 2026-09-28 operator plan. Shared typed vocabulary validates in `ess/ess-inputs.yaml`; reuse `entity.recording` coordinates, core lossless public values, and store provider/expectation types.\n\n## Scope\n\nOwn `ess/domains/{store,executor}.yaml`, corresponding components and authored scenario directories, `checks/ess-conformance/src/{store,executor}.rs`, and `docs/ess/{store,executor}-traceability.md`. Shared runner/manifest and production sources are integration-owned; no behavior corrections.\n\n## Named acceptance groups\n\nStore: absence/unavailability, stale writes, exact retry/conflicting global identity, memory atomic rollback and FileStore single-subject capability, reopen/corruption, nonadvancing observations, history/imported evidence/original receipts/complete snapshots, projections and library migration.\nExecutor: malformed and empty batches, duplicate IDs, transaction order and rollback, saved-definition recovery before load, changed retries, commit-then-uncertain and dropped response recovery, fork/merge checks, optional refusal recording versus malformed-input rejection.\n\nNative memory recorded store does not implement refusal recording or forked lineage. Supplied port fixtures may exercise real executor orchestration and must be labeled honestly; no invented native capability. Observe actual returns, histories, snapshots, receipts and provider traces. Independent authored expected values, isolated state, no boolean test wrapper. Retain a production mutation detected by a named scenario per domain, report/2 paired to exact suites, and integrate under the full repository gate.\n","document":{"events":[{"args":{"changes":{"scope":[{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/executor.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"checks/ess-conformance/src/store.rs"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"ess/domains/executor.yaml"},{"confidence":"cit